@lang en
IMPORT `msig-cgl-part-pco`

-- THE ANSWERS. Not a provision of the policy: this module asks the provisions encoded in
-- the other modules, in an order, and reports the first that decides.
--
--   1. Is the claim covered under a coverage part?  `the answer under ...`
--   2. How much does the Company pay for the occurrence?  `the most the Company pays ...`
--   3. Both together.  `what the Company pays ...`
--
-- ARM ORDER. The policy states a priority only twice: the Special Conditions "supersede
-- any other similar" clause, and the Institute Radioactive clause is "paramount". Neither
-- changes whether there is cover, because every arm after the insuring agreement is an
-- exclusion and any one of them defeats the claim. The order below is the ENCODING's:
-- the coverage part, the insured, the insuring agreement, the territory, the
-- jurisdiction, then (P&CO only) the claims-made conditions, then the part's own
-- exclusions in printed order, then the Special Conditions in printed order. It decides
-- only which reason is reported, and how few facts are needed to report it: L4 stops at
-- the first arm that decides.

§ `The answer on cover`

§§ `The date a harm is taken to occur`

-- In the P&CO part a claim in a Claim Series Event takes the series' date of occurrence
-- (src:768); every other claim is dated by its own harm (src:59, 164-166).
@ref src:59, 164-166, 768
GIVEN part  IS A `A coverage part`
      claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A DATE
`the date the harm is taken to occur under` part `, for` claim MEANS
    IF       part EQUALS `the Products and Completed Operations Liability Insurance Coverage Part`
         AND `Claim Series — the claim belongs to a Claim Series Event` claim
    THEN `Claim Series 3 — the date of occurrence of the series` claim
    ELSE `the date the harm is dated by` claim

§§ `Under the Comprehensive General Liability Insurance Coverage Part`

@export Whether a claim against an insured is covered under the Comprehensive General Liability Insurance Coverage Part of the MSIG Vietnam general liability policy, and if not, the clause that defeats it
@ref src:12-13, 46-49, 319-549, 700-977
GIVEN policy IS A `The policy as declared`    @desc The declarations and schedule: coverage parts, designation of the named insured, policy period, retroactive date, limits
      claim  IS A `A claim against an insured` @desc One claimant's claim against one insured, with the findings of fact on its record
GIVETH A `The answer on cover`
`the answer under the CGL Coverage Part` policy claim MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the declarations identify` `the Comprehensive General Liability Insurance Coverage Part` `as part of` policy
            THEN `not covered` `COVERAGE: the coverage part is not identified in the declarations`
        IF NOT `CGL II — the person claimed against is an insured` policy claim
            THEN `not covered` `PERSONS INSURED: the person claimed against is not an insured`
        IF `CGL II — the undesignated partnership or joint venture exclusion applies` claim
            THEN `not covered` `PERSONS INSURED: the conduct of a partnership or joint venture not designated as a named insured`
        IF NOT `for` claim `,` `the insured is legally obligated to pay the sums claimed as damages`
            THEN `not covered` `I: the insured is not legally obligated to pay the damages`
        IF NOT (`the harm is bodily injury` claim OR `the harm is property damage` claim)
            THEN `not covered` `I: the harm is neither bodily injury nor property damage as defined`
        IF NOT `it occurs during the policy period of` policy `on` (`the date the harm is taken to occur under` `the Comprehensive General Liability Insurance Coverage Part` `, for` claim)
            THEN `not covered` `I: the harm did not occur during the policy period`
        IF NOT `the harm was caused by an occurrence` claim
            THEN `not covered` `I: the harm was not caused by an occurrence`
        IF NOT `CGL IV — the harm occurs within the policy territory` claim
            THEN `not covered` `IV: the harm did not occur within the policy territory`
        IF `the Jurisdiction clause takes the judgement outside the indemnity` claim
            THEN `not covered` `JURISDICTION: the judgement was not delivered in the first instance by a court in Vietnam`
        IF `CGL exclusion (a) applies` claim THEN `not covered` `CGL exclusion (a): liability assumed under a contract`
        IF `CGL exclusion (b) applies` claim THEN `not covered` `CGL exclusion (b): automobiles and aircraft`
        IF `CGL exclusion (c) applies` claim THEN `not covered` `CGL exclusion (c): mobile equipment in a contest, and snowmobiles`
        IF `CGL exclusion (d) applies` claim THEN `not covered` `CGL exclusion (d): mobile equipment carried by an insured's automobile`
        IF `CGL exclusion (e) applies` claim THEN `not covered` `CGL exclusion (e): watercraft`
        IF `CGL exclusion (f) applies` claim THEN `not covered` `CGL exclusion (f): pollution`
        IF `CGL exclusion (g) applies` claim THEN `not covered` `CGL exclusion (g): war, for incidental contracts`
        IF `CGL exclusion (h) applies` claim THEN `not covered` `CGL exclusion (h): alcoholic beverages`
        IF `CGL exclusion (i) applies` claim THEN `not covered` `CGL exclusion (i): workmen's compensation and similar laws`
        IF `CGL exclusion (j) applies` claim THEN `not covered` `CGL exclusion (j): injury to the insured's employees`
        IF `CGL exclusion (k) applies` claim THEN `not covered` `CGL exclusion (k): property owned, used or controlled by the insured`
        IF `CGL exclusion (l) applies` claim THEN `not covered` `CGL exclusion (l): premises alienated by the named insured`
        IF `CGL exclusion (m) applies` claim THEN `not covered` `CGL exclusion (m): loss of use from delay or failure to perform`
        IF `CGL exclusion (n) applies` claim THEN `not covered` `CGL exclusion (n): damage to the named insured's products`
        IF `CGL exclusion (o) applies` claim THEN `not covered` `CGL exclusion (o): damage to the named insured's work`
        IF `CGL exclusion (p) applies` claim THEN `not covered` `CGL exclusion (p): withdrawal of products or work`
        IF `CGL exclusion (q) applies` claim THEN `not covered` `CGL exclusion (q): explosion, collapse and underground hazards`
        IF `the Completed Operations Hazard and Products Hazard Exclusion Clause applies` claim
            THEN `not covered` `COMPLETED OPERATIONS HAZARD AND PRODUCTS HAZARD EXCLUSION CLAUSE`
        IF `the special conditions for all coverage parts exclude` claim
            THEN `not covered` (`the special condition for all coverage parts that excludes` claim)
        OTHERWISE `covered`

§§ `Under the Products and Completed Operations Liability Insurance Coverage Part`

@export Whether a claim against an insured is covered under the Products and Completed Operations Liability Insurance Coverage Part of the MSIG Vietnam general liability policy, and if not, the clause that defeats it
@ref src:12-13, 46-49, 557-692, 700-977
GIVEN policy IS A `The policy as declared`    @desc The declarations and schedule: coverage parts, designation of the named insured, policy period, retroactive date, limits
      claim  IS A `A claim against an insured` @desc One claimant's claim against one insured, with the findings of fact on its record
GIVETH A `The answer on cover`
`the answer under the P&CO Coverage Part` policy claim MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the declarations identify` `the Products and Completed Operations Liability Insurance Coverage Part` `as part of` policy
            THEN `not covered` `COVERAGE: the coverage part is not identified in the declarations`
        IF NOT `P&CO II — the person claimed against is an insured` policy claim
            THEN `not covered` `PERSONS INSURED: the person claimed against is not an insured`
        IF `P&CO II — the undesignated partnership or joint venture exclusion applies` claim
            THEN `not covered` `PERSONS INSURED: the conduct of a partnership or joint venture not designated as a named insured`
        IF NOT `for` claim `,` `the insured is legally obligated to pay the sums claimed as damages`
            THEN `not covered` `I: the insured is not legally obligated to pay the damages`
        IF NOT (`the harm is bodily injury` claim OR `the harm is property damage` claim)
            THEN `not covered` `I: the harm is neither bodily injury nor property damage as defined`
        IF NOT `it occurs during the policy period of` policy `on` d
            THEN `not covered` `I: the harm did not occur during the policy period`
        IF NOT `the harm was caused by an occurrence` claim
            THEN `not covered` `I: the harm was not caused by an occurrence`
        IF NOT `P&CO I — the harm is within the completed operations hazard or the products hazard` claim
            THEN `not covered` `I: the harm is not within the completed operations hazard or the products hazard`
        IF NOT `P&CO IV — the harm occurs within the policy territory` claim
            THEN `not covered` `IV: the harm did not occur within the policy territory`
        IF `the Jurisdiction clause takes the judgement outside the indemnity` claim
            THEN `not covered` `JURISDICTION: the judgement was not delivered in the first instance by a court in Vietnam`
        IF NOT `Claims Made Basis 1 — the claim is made, or deemed made, during the policy period` policy claim
            THEN `not covered` `CLAIMS MADE BASIS 1: the claim was not made during the policy period`
        IF NOT `Claims Made Basis 1 — the harm, dated` d `, is sustained after the Retroactive Date of` policy
            THEN `not covered` `CLAIMS MADE BASIS 1: the harm was not sustained after the Retroactive Date`
        IF NOT `Claims Made Basis 1 — immediate notice has been given` claim
            THEN `not covered` `CLAIMS MADE BASIS 1: immediate notice was not given`
        IF NOT `Claims Made Basis 1 — the proviso on knowledge at the effective date holds` claim
            THEN `not covered` `CLAIMS MADE BASIS 1: the harm was known and foreseeable at the effective date`
        IF `Claims Made Basis 3 — the harm was caused before the Retroactive Date` claim
            THEN `not covered` `CLAIMS MADE BASIS 3: the harm was caused before the Retroactive Date`
        IF     `Claim Series — the claim belongs to a Claim Series Event` claim
           AND NOT `Claim Series 4 — the claim is made within 120 months of the first claim` claim
            THEN `not covered` `CLAIM SERIES 4: the claim was made more than 120 months after the first claim`
        IF `P&CO exclusion (a) applies` claim THEN `not covered` `P&CO exclusion (a): liability assumed under a contract`
        IF `P&CO exclusion (b) applies` claim THEN `not covered` `P&CO exclusion (b): alcoholic beverages`
        IF `P&CO exclusion (c) applies` claim THEN `not covered` `P&CO exclusion (c): workmen's compensation and similar laws`
        IF `P&CO exclusion (d) applies` claim THEN `not covered` `P&CO exclusion (d): injury to the insured's employees`
        IF `P&CO exclusion (e) applies` claim THEN `not covered` `P&CO exclusion (e): loss of use from delay or failure to perform`
        IF `P&CO exclusion (f) applies` claim THEN `not covered` `P&CO exclusion (f): damage to the named insured's products`
        IF `P&CO exclusion (g) applies` claim THEN `not covered` `P&CO exclusion (g): damage to the named insured's work`
        IF `P&CO exclusion (h) applies` claim THEN `not covered` `P&CO exclusion (h): withdrawal of products or work`
        IF `P&CO exclusion (i) applies` claim THEN `not covered` `P&CO exclusion (i): pollution`
        IF `the Business Risk Exclusion applies` claim THEN `not covered` `BUSINESS RISK EXCLUSION`
        IF `the special conditions for all coverage parts exclude` claim
            THEN `not covered` (`the special condition for all coverage parts that excludes` claim)
        OTHERWISE `covered`
    WHERE
        d MEANS `the date the harm is taken to occur under` `the Products and Completed Operations Liability Insurance Coverage Part` `, for` claim

§§ `The Special Conditions applicable to all coverage parts`

-- In printed order (src:781-977). The Combined Single Limit Endorsement, the Punitive
-- Damages Exclusion and the Ultimate Net Loss Clause are about amounts and are applied in
-- the next section; paragraph 1 of the Sistership clause is a duty.
@ref src:781-977
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the special conditions for all coverage parts exclude` claim MEANS
        `the Asbestos Exclusion applies` claim
    OR  `the Cyber Liability Exclusion applies` claim
    OR  `the Date Recognition Exception applies` claim
    OR  `the Electromagnetic Fields Exclusion applies` claim
    OR  `the Institute Radioactive Contamination Exclusion Clause applies` claim
    OR  `the Professional Liability Exclusion applies` claim
    OR  `the Sanction Limitation and Exclusion Clause applies` claim
    OR  `Sistership 2 — the exclusion applies` claim
    OR  `the War and Terrorism Exclusion applies` claim

@ref src:781-977
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A `A reason there is no cover`
`the special condition for all coverage parts that excludes` claim MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Asbestos Exclusion applies` claim                       THEN `ASBESTOS EXCLUSION`
        IF `the Cyber Liability Exclusion applies` claim                THEN `CYBER LIABILITY EXCLUSION`
        IF `the Date Recognition Exception applies` claim               THEN `DATE RECOGNITION EXCEPTION`
        IF `the Electromagnetic Fields Exclusion applies` claim         THEN `ELECTROMAGNETIC FIELDS EXCLUSION`
        IF `the Institute Radioactive Contamination Exclusion Clause applies` claim
            THEN `INSTITUTE RADIOACTIVE CONTAMINATION, CHEMICAL, BIOLOGICAL, BIOCHEMICAL AND ELECTROMAGNETIC WEAPONS EXCLUSION CLAUSE`
        IF `the Professional Liability Exclusion applies` claim         THEN `PROFESSIONAL LIABILITY EXCLUSION`
        IF `the Sanction Limitation and Exclusion Clause applies` claim THEN `SANCTION LIMITATION AND EXCLUSION CLAUSE`
        IF `Sistership 2 — the exclusion applies` claim                 THEN `SISTERSHIP EXCLUSION CLAUSE`
        OTHERWISE `WAR AND TERRORISM EXCLUSION`

@ref src:12-13
GIVEN part   IS A `A coverage part`
      policy IS A `The policy as declared`
      claim  IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A `The answer on cover`
`the answer under` part `, for` policy `and` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER part
    WHEN `the Comprehensive General Liability Insurance Coverage Part`             THEN `the answer under the CGL Coverage Part` policy claim
    WHEN `the Products and Completed Operations Liability Insurance Coverage Part` THEN `the answer under the P&CO Coverage Part` policy claim

§ `The amount the Company pays`

§§ `The ultimate net loss`

-- The limits apply to the ultimate net loss (Ultimate Net Loss Clause 1, src:923-924),
-- taken as operative over Supplementary Payments (fork F4). Left out of it, each by the
-- clause that says so:
--   * the punitive part of an award (Punitive Damages Exclusion): its own field, never
--     added;
--   * voluntary payments (Condition 3(c), "at his own cost") and the cost of withdrawal or
--     preventive measures (Sistership paragraph 3): their own fields, never added;
--   * in the CGL part, first aid expenses where the harm is due to war (CGL (g)(2)).
@ref src:226-227, 378-383, 888-889, 914-916, 923-949
GIVEN part  IS A `A coverage part`
      claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
      sums  IS A `The sums for one occurrence`
      rates IS A `Rates of exchange into dong`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the ultimate net loss counted under` part `, for` claim `, of` sums `at` rates MEANS
        `the ultimate net loss of` sums `at` rates
    MINUS (IF       part EQUALS `the Comprehensive General Liability Insurance Coverage Part`
               AND `CGL exclusion (g)(2) takes out the first aid expenses` claim
           THEN `Ultimate Net Loss 2(d)` sums
           ELSE 0)

§§ `The limits`

@ref src:512-540, 673-683
GIVEN part  IS A `A coverage part`
      claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the bodily injury aggregate applies under` part `, for` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER part
    WHEN `the Comprehensive General Liability Insurance Coverage Part`             THEN `CGL III Coverage A — the occurrence falls under the bodily injury aggregate` claim
    WHEN `the Products and Completed Operations Liability Insurance Coverage Part` THEN `P&CO III Coverage A — the occurrence falls under the bodily injury aggregate` claim

@ref src:520-540, 681-683
GIVEN part  IS A `A coverage part`
      claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a property damage aggregate applies under` part `, for` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER part
    WHEN `the Comprehensive General Liability Insurance Coverage Part`             THEN `CGL III Coverage B — the occurrence falls under a property damage aggregate` claim
    WHEN `the Products and Completed Operations Liability Insurance Coverage Part` THEN `P&CO III Coverage B — the occurrence falls under the property damage aggregate` claim

-- Under SEPARATE limits (III as printed) the damages for bodily injury go to Coverage A's
-- limit and those for property damage to Coverage B's. The other sums in the ultimate net
-- loss (defence, bonds, first aid, the insured's expenses) are "inclusive in the
-- applicable limit" without saying which, where one occurrence causes both. Where the
-- occurrence causes only one kind, they go with it; where it causes neither (a groundless
-- suit), with the kind of harm the claim alleges; where it causes both, the answer is
-- declined (NOTES.md, fork F11; finding X5).
@ref src:18, 504-540, 665-683, 923-924
GIVEN part   IS A `A coverage part`
      policy IS A `The policy as declared`
      claim  IS A `A claim against an insured`
      sums   IS A `The sums for one occurrence`
      rates  IS A `Rates of exchange into dong`
      paid   IS A `Amounts already paid under the aggregate limits`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most the Company pays for the occurrence under` part `, for` policy `,` claim `,` sums `,` rates `,` paid MEANS
    CONSIDER policy's `the limits stated in the schedule`
    WHEN `a combined single limit` occ agg THEN
        min `ultimate net loss`
            (`Combined Single Limit — the cap, each occurrence` occ `, aggregate` agg `, already paid` (paid's `under the combined aggregate`) `, for` claim)
    WHEN `separate limits for bodily injury and property damage` bo ba po pa THEN
        BRANCH
            IF   bi GREATER THAN 0 AND pd GREATER THAN 0 AND `the other sums` GREATER THAN 0
            THEN `the Policy does not say which limit absorbs the other sums when one occurrence causes both bodily injury and property damage`
            IF   bi GREATER THAN 0 OR (pd EQUALS 0 AND `the harm is bodily injury` claim)
            THEN    min (bi PLUS `the other sums`) (`cap A` bo ba)
                 +  min pd (`cap B` po pa)
            OTHERWISE
                    min bi (`cap A` bo ba)
                 +  min (pd PLUS `the other sums`) (`cap B` po pa)
    WHERE
        `ultimate net loss` MEANS `the ultimate net loss counted under` part `, for` claim `, of` sums `at` rates
        bi MEANS sums's `damages because of bodily injury`
        pd MEANS sums's `damages because of property damage`
        `the other sums` MEANS `ultimate net loss` MINUS bi MINUS pd
        `cap A` o a MEANS
            `the cap of` o `each occurrence, and of` a `aggregate less` (paid's `under the bodily injury aggregate`) `if it applies:` (`the bodily injury aggregate applies under` part `, for` claim)
        `cap B` o a MEANS
            `the cap of` o `each occurrence, and of` a `aggregate less` (paid's `under the property damage aggregate that applies`) `if it applies:` (`a property damage aggregate applies under` part `, for` claim)

@ref src:18, 504-540, 665-683
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Policy does not say which limit absorbs the other sums when one occurrence causes both bodily injury and property damage` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Policy does not say which limit absorbs the other sums when one occurrence causes both bodily injury and property damage"

-- "the Company shall not be obligated to pay any claim or judgement or to defend any suit
-- after the applicable limit of the Company's liability has been exhausted by payment of
-- judgements or settlements" (src:335-336, 574-575).
@ref src:332-336, 571-575
GIVEN part   IS A `A coverage part`
      policy IS A `The policy as declared`
      claim  IS A `A claim against an insured`
      paid   IS A `Amounts already paid under the aggregate limits`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the applicable limit is exhausted under` part `, for` policy `,` claim `,` paid MEANS
    CONSIDER policy's `the limits stated in the schedule`
    WHEN `a combined single limit` occ agg THEN
            `Combined Single Limit — the aggregate applies to the occurrence` claim
        AND paid's `under the combined aggregate` AT LEAST agg
    WHEN `separate limits for bodily injury and property damage` bo ba po pa THEN
        IF   `the harm is bodily injury` claim
        THEN     `the bodily injury aggregate applies under` part `, for` claim
             AND paid's `under the bodily injury aggregate` AT LEAST ba
        ELSE     `a property damage aggregate applies under` part `, for` claim
             AND paid's `under the property damage aggregate that applies` AT LEAST pa

§§ `Cover and amount together`

-- Layer 1 then layer 2: nothing if the claim is not covered, else the most the limits
-- allow. Other insurance (Condition 5) may lower the Company's share further; it takes
-- the other policies as input and is applied by the caller to this figure.
@export The most the MSIG Vietnam general liability policy pays for one occurrence under a coverage part: zero if the claim is not covered, otherwise the ultimate net loss within the applicable limits
@ref src:18, 319-549, 557-692, 794-814, 919-949
GIVEN part   IS A `A coverage part`                                 @desc Which coverage part the claim is made under
      policy IS A `The policy as declared`                          @desc The declarations and schedule
      claim  IS A `A claim against an insured`                      @desc The claim that stands for the occurrence, with its findings
      sums   IS A `The sums for one occurrence`                     @desc Damages and supplementary sums for the whole occurrence, in dong
      rates  IS A `Rates of exchange into dong`                     @desc Dong per US dollar and per Singapore dollar, for the bail bond and earnings caps
      paid   IS A `Amounts already paid under the aggregate limits` @desc What has already been paid out of each aggregate limit, in dong
GIVETH A NUMBER
`what the Company pays under` part `, for` policy `,` claim `,` sums `,` rates `,` paid MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer under` part `, for` policy `and` claim
    WHEN `covered`       THEN `the most the Company pays for the occurrence under` part `, for` policy `,` claim `,` sums `,` rates `,` paid
    WHEN `not covered` r THEN 0
